Name: glib
URL: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib
Version: 2.90.1
Revision: e05063ccc6c8f222465a1080927f4c14349f3de6
Update Mechanism: Autoroll
License: LGPL-2.1
License File: LICENSE
Shipped: no
Security Critical: no

Description:
Low-level core library that forms the basis for projects such as GTK+ and GNOME.

This is only used in tests.

Local Modifications:
None.

Generated code (enum types, D-Bus code, and visibility and version macros) is
generated at build time from the in-tree glib using the codegen wrappers and
templates in this directory (see codegen.gni). Only the headers produced by
meson's host configuration checks are checked in, under include/. config.h and
glibconfig.h are checked in as templates with the version-dependent values
replaced by placeholders, which are filled in at build time from
src/meson.build, so they don't change when glib is rolled.

LICENSE is the standard text of the LGPL 2.1, which glib is licensed under
(LGPL-2.1-or-later). It is checked in instead of using src/COPYING, which has
the same terms but is reformatted such that Chromium's license checker doesn't
recognize it. It doesn't need to be updated when glib is rolled.

This is updated by an autoroller that tracks stable (even minor) upstream
release tags. Point releases only need a DEPS update. If a roll fails, e.g. for
a new minor version, take over the roll CL and:
1. Add any new sources and generated-code inputs from the upstream meson.build
   files to BUILD.gn.
2. If upstream changed its configuration checks, run on_update.sh and check in
   the regenerated headers under include/.
